---
title: Setup and troubleshooting
description: Download preview.2, select the matching SDK and resolve setup problems.
sidebar:
  order: 1
---

## Download preview.2

Get the [Windows 64-bit ZIP and checksum](https://github.com/gmoddev/LUI/releases/tag/sdk-v0.1.0-preview.2).
Extract the whole archive, then select its `LUI-SDK-0.1.0-preview.2` folder with
**LUI: Choose SDK**. Install the included extension **0.1.7** from `Editor/LUI.vsix`
using VS Code's **Install from VSIX** command. The SDK tools are included; a global
.NET SDK or C++ runtime was not needed on the selected Windows test recipient.

Keep old SDK folders for projects pinned to them. Do not mix files between versions
or change a project's inventory digest to silence a mismatch.

## Verify the download

```powershell
Get-FileHash ./LUI-SDK-Windows-x64-0.1.0-preview.2.zip -Algorithm SHA256
```

Compare it with the release's `.sha256` file. The expected ZIP hash is:

```text
6e89f007e8012367c5ef183d46d50f41c3909c3b1d1e918e4b727cf842676d49
```

A checksum verifies unchanged bytes, not publisher identity. This is an unsigned,
experimental preview. Do not disable Windows protections to run a download.

## Check and create an app

From the extracted SDK folder:

```powershell
./lui.cmd doctor
./lui.cmd new MyApp
./lui.cmd check ./MyApp/lui.json
```

Open `MyApp` in VS Code, select this SDK and use **LUI: Run App**. Save project
files and use **LUI: Restart App** after changes. Restart discards app memory, so
save documents inside your app first too. Native apps do not restart on save.

## Common problems

| Problem | Recovery |
| --- | --- |
| Commands are missing | Install this SDK's `Editor/LUI.vsix`. |
| SDK cannot be found | Select the folder containing `SdkManifest.json`, not `Cli`. |
| Inventory mismatch | Extract the complete original ZIP to a new folder. |
| Project pin mismatch | Select the exact SDK recorded in `LuiToolchain.json`. |
| A new source is excluded | Use Add File to Project, review and save the manifest, then check types. |
| Native app shows old code | Save project files and use Restart App. |
| Setup or capability failure | Read LUI Preview Output and the [capability guide](../capabilities/). |

See the [workflow](../workflow/) and [tested scope](../platforms/). Windows 11,
physical input methods, ordinary downloaded-file trust and signing remain open.
